title The number I typed into my own header
prompt the baton -- COPAL, lane amphora and bron-resins, next agent-doable lap
rota lap 4202, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees: cut and stop, read through vision. Its threshold asks a lap to look straight at the thing most laps route around, and the thing here was last lap's own sentence: a guard header that named its blind spot with two numbers a hand had counted at a prompt.
think Opened cold. The roster pass was killed at exit 144 partway through the alphabet with every guard it reached green, so this lap closes on a full hot pass rather than on a cold receipt.
think The open printed stashed_entries=8 before it printed a guard, which is %499's shape from the receiving end. Read all eight before concluding anything: every path in every stash resolves in HEAD, and the files that differ are elder drafts of work that later landed. Nothing lost, one whole reading spent -- and that is the honest answer rather than the disappointing one.
think Then the lane's own fences, and they hold: the resin catalog gates uncatalogued, orphan and duplicate at zero and states its one .md exception rather than hiding it; the amphora bounds reader declares its order relations both ways. So the fire lap turned on what I wrote yesterday.
think prose_register_scan.sh names its Door roster rather than discovering it, on purpose. Last lap I wrote the population that clause leaves out into the scan's header as prose -- 80 front doors readable, 30 over the ceiling -- both counted once by hand at a shell prompt that left nothing behind.
think Writing the reading the header described is what found the fault. The scan now counts 119 tracked front doors, 80 readable, and 28 unrostered over the ceiling, naming each by path and share.
obs THE GAP IS A CATEGORY ERROR RATHER THAN DRIFT, and that is the finding. Two of my thirty were tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_prose_close_elder/README.md and its count sibling -- frozen plants whose own first line reads kept exactly as it shipped, and which a control reads byte for byte. A lane sweeping either would break the guard rather than mend a door.
obs So the repair reads past tools/fixtures/ and vendor/ by name, each with its reason written beside it. A count nobody can act on is what the resin catalog names every file to avoid, and a hand-counted population cannot tell an actionable name from a frozen one.
obs The reading is reported and never gated, because a page that agreed to nothing must not refuse the tree. Proving that by watching the live tree would hold only while the tree happens to carry a candidate, so the proof is a pen: one over-ceiling page off the roster is named and the verdict still reads ok, and the same bytes one roster line later refuse at door_over_ceiling=1. One roster line apart, so the report is told from the gate.
obs Disarming the roster-exclusion line reds the third leg on metal, so it is told from a bypass. Control 13 behaviors to 16.
obs Both pins were at their ceilings before a byte moved. REDS stood 582 bytes free, so a folded row made the room -- %576 at the first park, and %578 by the time this draft actually landed; the card stood 53 free, so the elder COPAL account folded and the new one was written five times against living_pin_max_bytes until it fit.
obs THE HOT PASS CAUGHT FOUR REDS AND ALL FOUR WERE THIS ROUND'S OWN. reds_ledger_headline read 581 against a measured 582, since a new row moves a count the page recites; reds_ledger_monotone read the same drift one instrument over, so two guards fired on one root. The repair is the write script the refusal names.
obs THE THIRD IS THE ONE WORTH KEEPING. fold_shelf_link refused the new archive account at fold_depth_lost: the elder block I copied into it carried `archive/20260907-170601_...`, correct from the card and one directory too deep from a shelf that already stands inside archive/. A fold moves bytes, and a link written for the old depth resolves nowhere from the new one.
obs THE FOURTH READ MY OWN NEW LINE. instrument_refusal counts `[ x ] || { ...; }` as a fallback value standing in for an answer, so the bounded printout is an `if` block now. The sibling line above it survives because a bare `||` with no brace group is a different shape -- a guard reading spellings rather than intentions, which is the only kind that can be trusted.
